-- X23 (SHADOW-SEMANTICS S1-PRELUDE (b)) -- the denotation assertion, no shadow present.
--
-- x19 through x22 all put a collision or a boundary in the program.  This cell removes both
-- and asserts the property the recovery spellings exist to have in the FIRST place: an
-- aliased or renamed prelude name denotes THE SAME FUNCTION as the bare one.
--
--   PINNED: `True` -- the conjunction, so a cell that bound a different `isEven` (or bound
--     nothing and defaulted) cannot pass by getting one comparison right.
--   Both recovery spellings appear, because they take different paths: the module alias
--     stays dotted through inference, the member rename is rewritten to the origin name
--     before it.  A cell naming only one grades only one path.
--   The `7` comparison is present so the assertion is not satisfied by an `isEven` that
--     returns a constant.
--
-- An exit-code-only reading of this cell is worth nothing: every way of getting the
-- denotation wrong here still exits 0 and prints `False`.
import core as C
import core.{isEven as even2}

main =
  println
    (C.isEven 4 == isEven 4 && even2 4 == isEven 4 && C.isEven 7 == isEven 7)
